  "notes": "West leads the ♠2 against 6♠. West's trump lead is won by South. South's only possible losers are in the diamond suit. South's plan should involve ruffing at least 1 of his small diamonds in the dummy.\n\nIf South cashes a top diamond at trick 2, he might think about crossing to the ♥A before leading a second diamond intending to play the ♦K unless East ruffs. This is a safety play against East holding a singleton diamond and 3 trumps.\n\nHowever, if East follows suit and South tries to win the trick, he will go down when West is the defender with 3 trumps and a singleton diamond. West will ruff and play his last trump leaving South with a certain diamond loser.\n\nOnce the first round of diamonds lives, South can guard against a singleton diamond and 3 spades in either hand by ducking a round of diamonds. South will have no trouble ruffing his other diamond loser in dummy.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West leads the ♠2 against 6♠. West's trump lead is won by South. South's only possible losers are in the diamond suit. South's plan should involve ruffing at least 1 of his small diamonds in the dummy.",
